<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss March trade surplus revised down.</title>
<headline>Swiss March trade surplus revised down.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's trade surplus in March was revised to 0.2 million Swiss francs from a surplus of 3.1 million first reported, the Federal Customs Office said.</p>
<p>It gave these revised figures:</p>
<p> Balance  (million Sfr)	     +0.2</p>
<p> Imports  (million Sfr)	  8,331.2</p>
<p> Exports  (million Sfr)	  8,331.4</p>
<p>Note - Provisional figures showed a surplus of 3.1 million on imports of 8,317.0 million and exports of 8,320.2 million. Figues exclude precious metals, precious stones, art objects and antiques.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
